# Raw request paths whose reading by the dashboard's server is recorded in paths.json — by
# paths.mjs, which runs the built server itself — and compared with the gateway's reading of
# the same paths (internal/gateway/dash_paths_test.go). One path per line, sent as written; a
# line beginning with # is a comment (a request path begins with /).
#
# This file holds the fixed lines. paths.mjs adds, for every route of the built route tree,
# the route's plain form and its mechanical forms: a dot-dot segment before it, plain and
# percent-encoded; static segments in capitals; a doubled slash; a backslash, an encoded
# backslash and an encoded slash for a slash; a control character; another project's ref in
# each position, in both letter cases; double encoding; a letter that only folds to ASCII
# when lower-cased; an overlong encoding; a # after each segment, at the end and before a
# dot-dot; a trailing slash; a trailing encoded space (alone, doubled, before an empty and a
# non-empty query, as a segment of its own, behind a dot segment); a percent-encoded letter;
# and, under /api, an encoded space beside the first segment and a first segment that only
# decodes twice. So a route the build gains has its vectors without an edit here, and
# paths.json changes with the route tree.
# It also adds every octet, percent-encoded, at the edges of three paths it chooses from the
# route tree: the end of the path, a segment of its own, each side of the first segment,
# behind a dot segment, with and without an empty query. A parser that strips, resolves or
# cuts at an octet there is seen, whatever the octet.
#
# Two refs stand in the vectors: aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa1 is the project of the request,
# bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb2 another project's.
/
/api
/api/ai
/api/mcp
/Api
/API
/api/Ai
/api/AI
/api/Mcp
/API/MCP
/api/mcp#
